# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even in a Windows working copy.
#
# These are edited on Windows and run on Linux, and they are as likely to reach
# the cluster by rsync from the working copy as by a fresh clone. A CRLF copy
# fails at the shebang — `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M` — which reads
# like a broken cluster rather than a line-ending problem.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sbatch text eol=lf
